# EVERYTHING IN THE BUILD CONTEXT ENDS UP IN THE IMAGE.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . /opt/app`, and the image is pushed to a registry by CI. Without
# this file a local build baked `.env` — the Discord bot token and the database credentials —
# plus `.env.prod` and every `.env.backup-*` straight into a published layer, where deleting
# the file later does not remove it. CI is spared only because `.env` is gitignored and a
# checkout never has it; a developer building on their own machine is not.

# Secrets. The example is the only one that may ship.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# History, including anything ever committed.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Installed fresh inside the image, and copying the host's build is both slower and wrong when
# the platform differs. package-lock.json deliberately DOES ship: it is the only thing pinning
# discord.js to the version whose source the postinstall patch knows how to rewrite.
node_modules

# Nothing the running bot reads.
__tests__
coverage
.jest
*.log
logs
.idea
crowdin.yml
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
RELEASE.md
CLAUDE.md
